@startuml repository-pattern
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 11
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 25
top to bottom direction


class PlantAppManager {
  +plant_repo: PlantRepository
  +schedule_repo: CareScheduleRepository
  +log_repo: ActionLogRepository
  +user_repo: UserRepository
}


abstract class PlantRepository {
  {abstract} +save(plant: Plant): None
  {abstract} +get_by_id(plant_id: int): Plant | None
  {abstract} +find_all(): List[Plant]
  {abstract} +find_by_user(user_id: int): List[Plant]
  {abstract} +delete(plant_id: int): None
}


abstract class CareScheduleRepository {
  {abstract} +save(schedule: CareSchedule): None
  {abstract} +get_by_id(schedule_id: int): CareSchedule | None
  {abstract} +find_by_plant(plant_id: int): List[CareSchedule]
  {abstract} +find_by_plant_and_care_type(plant_id: int, care_type: str): CareSchedule | None
  {abstract} +delete(schedule_id: int): None
}


abstract class ActionLogRepository {
  {abstract} +save(log: ActionLog): None
  {abstract} +get_by_id(log_id: int): ActionLog | None
  {abstract} +find_by_plant(plant_id: int): List[ActionLog]
  {abstract} +delete(log_id: int): None
}

abstract class UserRepository {
  {abstract} +save(user: User): None
  {abstract} +get_by_id(user_id: int): User | None
  {abstract} +find_by_username(username: str): User | None
  {abstract} +delete(user_id: int): None
}

class InMemoryPlantRepository {
  -_store: dict
  -_next_id: int
}


class InMemoryCareScheduleRepository {
  -_store: dict
  -_next_id: int
}


class InMemoryActionLogRepository {
  -_store: dict
  -_next_id: int
}

class InMemoryUserRepository {
  -_store: dict
  -_next_id: int
}


class Plant {
  +id: int | None
  +user_id: int
  +name: str
  +species: str
  +location: str
  +created_at: str
}

class CareSchedule {
  +id: int | None
  +plant_id: int
  +care_type: str
  +interval_days: int
}


class ActionLog {
  +id: int | None
  +plant_id: int
  +care_type: str
  +performed_at: str
  +notes: str
}

class User {
  +id: int | None
  +username: str
  +password_hash: str
}


' ── Dependency Inversion: Manager → abstract interfaces ──
PlantAppManager --> PlantRepository
PlantAppManager --> CareScheduleRepository
PlantAppManager --> ActionLogRepository
PlantAppManager --> UserRepository


' ── Implementations ─────────────────────────────────────
PlantRepository <|-- InMemoryPlantRepository
CareScheduleRepository <|-- InMemoryCareScheduleRepository
ActionLogRepository <|-- InMemoryActionLogRepository
UserRepository <|-- InMemoryUserRepository


' ── Repository returns domain models ─────────────────────
PlantRepository ..> Plant : returns
CareScheduleRepository ..> CareSchedule : returns
ActionLogRepository ..> ActionLog : returns
UserRepository ..> User : returns

' ── Column layout (left → right) ─────────────────────────
PlantRepository -[hidden]right- CareScheduleRepository
CareScheduleRepository -[hidden]right- ActionLogRepository
ActionLogRepository -[hidden]right- UserRepository
InMemoryPlantRepository -[hidden]right- InMemoryCareScheduleRepository
InMemoryCareScheduleRepository -[hidden]right- InMemoryActionLogRepository
InMemoryActionLogRepository -[hidden]right- InMemoryUserRepository
Plant -[hidden]right- CareSchedule
CareSchedule -[hidden]right- ActionLog
ActionLog -[hidden]right- User
PlantRepository -[hidden]down- InMemoryPlantRepository
InMemoryPlantRepository -[hidden]down- Plant
CareScheduleRepository -[hidden]down- InMemoryCareScheduleRepository
InMemoryCareScheduleRepository -[hidden]down- CareSchedule
ActionLogRepository -[hidden]down- InMemoryActionLogRepository
InMemoryActionLogRepository -[hidden]down- ActionLog
UserRepository -[hidden]down- InMemoryUserRepository
InMemoryUserRepository -[hidden]down- User

note as N1
Für diese User Story habe ich ein Klassendiagramm gewählt,
weil hier vor allem die Struktur des Codes verändert wird.

Die User Story führt abstrakte Repository-Klassen und konkrete
InMemory-Implementierungen ein. Das Diagramm zeigt, dass
PlantAppManager nur von den abstrakten Repository-Klassen abhängt
und nicht direkt von den InMemory-Klassen.

Außerdem wird sichtbar, dass die ID-Vergabe nicht mehr in den
Modellklassen liegt, sondern in der save()-Methode der Repositories.

Ein Sequenz- oder Aktivitätsdiagramm wäre hier weniger passend,
weil kein neuer Ablauf modelliert wird, sondern neue Klassen und
ihre Beziehungen.
end note

@enduml